## WHAT THE GATE FOUND (RELAYED: `briefs/2026-11-15_B1564_verify/VERDICT.md`, read whole; your commission is these findings)
- **F1 (Major).** On UNCHANGED code with `DOTNET_PROCESSOR_COUNT=4` (the size of a hosted runner's pool; a probe on this 18-CPU box, not a hosted run) the rows went red in 4 of 35 runs: the clause-5 16-step row (`1/64 ... (max 2688 ms)`, `64/64 ... (max 2527 ms)`) and the poll row (`24/24 ... (max 2541 ms)`, `(max 2664 ms)`); in every red the WHOLE group arrived late together (median = max): one pool stall of 25 to 170 ms past the 500 ms margin, not a slow product path. Default pool: 0 red in 26. 2-CPU pool: 0 red in 5. `FreeThreads = 8` at `LaneMAPollAndHandOffTests.cs:20`; `[InlineData(16, 12)]` at `LaneMAClause5Tests.cs:64`; the hand-off row has no `LeaveFree`. Hosted CI runs the rows on every push to main, so a flake here is a flaky gate: **that is the bar.**
- **F2 (Minor).** `LaneMAParkedPool.cs:32` (`int toPark = Math.Max(Math.Max(ThreadPool.ThreadCount, minimum) - free, 0);`): "leave N free" is a CEILING, not a guarantee: when the pool holds no more than N threads it parks 0 (printed `0 pool threads parked` in a run), so the free count the row depends on varies with earlier tests and machine size. DERIVED by the drafter: the group's fixture sets the pool minimum to `ProcessorCount + 8` (`OverlayResidueTests.B54.cs:386`), i.e. 10 at 2 CPUs and 12 at 4, so `LeaveFree(12)` parks nothing on a cold 4-CPU pool and the burst runs on threads the pool must INJECT (about one per 0.5 s above its minimum, the class remark above `OverlayTimingPool`, `OverlayResidueTests.B54.cs`, which says a starved pool above its minimum adds one about every 0.5 s).
- **F3 (Minor).** The round-1 STATUS says the existing stage row goes red under m0 in 3 of 3 runs (2652 to 2656 ms, "one of four, thin"); the gate ran the four existing rows under m0 3 times and got 0 red (max 2034 ms). **Correct the claim in YOUR STATUS (no repo change; see Step 7).**
- I1 to I4 (Info): the hand-off row under m2 is deterministic here (13 of 24 in 5 of 5), stronger than the builder said; the kit's one-line m1 does not build under warnings-as-errors (use the `await Task.CompletedTask;` form below); raising free threads does not hide a product timing problem (harness capacity only); main moved web-only, merge-tree clean.

